From f81390fbe202ff6a4c27500b02dc1b9d1941712e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:47:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 858/860] perf(dsv41): expert-centric prefill streaming for
 slot cache

When an offloaded MoE batch touches more non-static experts than dynamic_slots,
token-order window partitioning splits a prefill chunk into hundreds of small
windows and re-reads cold experts from NVMe 10x-30x per layer with a CUDA
stream synchronization on every window.

Sweep active experts once per layer in ascending LBA order instead: Pass 0
runs all resident experts (static + warm dynamic) with zero NVMe I/O, and
Passes 1..K stream remaining cold experts once each in dynamic_slots batches
with role-major w13/w2 overlap, exact plan.out_dtype FP32 accumulation, and
shared-expert folding before the single final cast. Active by default on
slot-cached shapes (VLLM_DS41_EXPERT_PREFILL_MODE=token selects legacy
token-order windowing). Zero code path impact when VLLM_DS41_EXPERT_SLOTS=0.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Lifts TP=2 prefill from 259/236 to 4,597/4,897 tok/s (17.8x-20.8x) and TP=1 prefill from 24.4 to 333 (1K) / 1,229 (8K) / 2,114 (32K) tok/s.
Quality: Exact FP32 cross-batch accumulation under TileLangExperts (plan.out_dtype=float32); verified LRU 5/5 on live TP=1 and TP=2-direct.
Tests: pytest tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_expert_slots.py
Upstream-status: Local expert slot cache prefill optimization.
